// Ownership: an `own` value read in BOTH arms of an `if` is ONE consume on
// the taken path (the arms are ALTERNATIVES — exactly one runs), and an
// `own` param in one function is unrelated to the same-named param in the
// next. Before if/match bracketed their arms as BAlternative and the consume
// ledger scoped per function body, `tally` floored on its two arms and
// `total` floored on `buf` left "used" by `tally` — the cross-function false
// positive. Both are clean now; no runtime linked, so the gate tests only
// the affine ledger.
fn keep(x) with Pure = x

fn tally(own buf, i) with Pure =
  if i < 0 { keep(buf) }
  else { keep(buf) }

fn total(own buf) with Pure = keep(buf)

fn main() = tally(10, -1) + total(20)
